From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maksym Vasylchuk <max@buzztv.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] aesv8-armx.pl: emit the .Lrcon pointer load on all 32-bit
 flavours

aes_v8_set_encrypt_key loads the AES round constants through $ptr, which
on 32-bit ARM is set up by an "adr r3,.Lrcon". That instruction is emitted
only when the perlasm flavour name matches /32/, but the android-arm target
in Configurations/15-android.conf uses flavour "void", so the load is
silently dropped while the rest of the function is emitted unchanged. r3
then still holds the -2 (bad key size) sentinel from the argument checks
above, and the first vld1.32 from it faults:

  aes_v8_set_encrypt_key:
    mvn     r3, #0x1
    ...
    vld1.32 {d2,d3,d4,d5}, [r3]!

Every AES operation that reaches the ARMv8 crypto-extension code path on a
32-bit Android build therefore crashes, unless the application disables
hardware crypto entirely with OPENSSL_armcap=0.

Test !~ /64/ instead, which is what every other 32-bit-only block in this
file already does, so the flavour name no longer has to contain "32".
---
 crypto/aes/asm/aesv8-armx.pl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crypto/aes/asm/aesv8-armx.pl b/crypto/aes/asm/aesv8-armx.pl
index 1650a0dd6f..1c31d3ad1c 100755
--- a/crypto/aes/asm/aesv8-armx.pl
+++ b/crypto/aes/asm/aesv8-armx.pl
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@ $code.=<<___	if ($flavour =~ /64/);
 	adrp	$ptr,.Lrcon
 	add	$ptr,$ptr,:lo12:.Lrcon
 ___
-$code.=<<___	if ($flavour =~ /32/);
+$code.=<<___	if ($flavour !~ /64/);
 	adr	$ptr,.Lrcon
 ___
 $code.=<<___;
